<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.3 </span>Code-mixed Sarcasm Fine-tuned DistilBERT</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The confusion matrix in table <a href="#A1.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ A.3.3 Code-mixed Sarcasm Fine-tuned DistilBERT ‣ A.3. Confusion Matrices ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Small Wins Big: Comparing Large Language Models and Domain Fine-Tuned Models for Sarcasm Detection in Code-Mixed Hinglish Text" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows the performance of the classical model fine-tuned on code-mixed Sarcasm data. It is evident that an optimal trade-off between precision and recall results in this model being outperforming all other models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Confusion matrix for the best performing DistilBERT model</figcaption>
